        "params": {
          "text": "**SP07 \u2014 Which filter resonates?**  \n**Does the measured response match the actual discrete filter?** Run **64 s at 64 Hz**.  \nBoth DC gains are 1. The resonant peak is about 2.99 near 0.625 Hz. Low-pass starts one sample after the pulse; resonant starts two later.  \nChange damping factor 1.6 \u2192 3.2; predict a lower resonance. Capture 64 s for the decaying tail; Scope: inspect 0\u201310 s.  \n[Open SP07 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP07-filter-transfer/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT teaching materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_lec11/) \u00b7 [S7 timing and integrators](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/INTEGRATORS.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1789,
          "height": 300,
          "font_size": 20
        }
      }
    ]
